<title>USA: Philip Morris execs to be quizzed on talks.</title>
<headline>Philip Morris execs to be quizzed on talks.</headline>
<byline>Michael Connor</byline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two words sure to be heard at Thursday's annual shareholder meeting by Philip Morris Cos Inc are &quot;no comment.&quot;</p>
<p>Questions about the top tobacco group's role in historic settlement talks that may end in a cigarette-industry payout of $300 billion or more are certain to arise when Chief Executive Geoffrey Bible meets shareholders at Philip Morris' sprawling manufacturing plant in Richmond, Virginia, activists and industry analysts said.</p>
</text>
